      "source": [
        "## 🔮 Prediction Protocol — From 3M Yield to Full Curve\n",
        "\n",
        "### The Problem\n",
        "\n",
        "On a test day, we only observe the **3-month yield** $y_{\\text{obs}}(0.25)$. We want to predict the 6M, 9M, 1Y, and 2Y yields.\n",
        "\n",
        "### The Solution — Invert the Yield Formula\n",
        "\n",
        "Because the CIR yield is affine in $r_t$, we can rearrange the formula algebraically to *solve for* $r_t$:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$y(\\tau) = \\frac{B(\\tau) \\cdot r_t - \\ln A(\\tau)}{\\tau}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\Downarrow$$\n",
        "\n",
        "$$r_t = \\frac{y_{\\text{obs}} \\cdot \\tau + \\ln A(\\tau)}{B(\\tau)} \\quad \\text{(using } \\tau = 0.25 \\text{)}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "Then plug this recovered $r_t$ into the model to predict all other yields:\n",
        "\n",
        "$$\\hat{y}(\\tau_j) = \\frac{B(\\tau_j) \\cdot r_t - \\ln A(\\tau_j)}{\\tau_j} \\quad \\text{for } j = 6\\text{M}, 9\\text{M}, 1\\text{Y}, 2\\text{Y}$$\n",
        "\n",
        "**Important:** This is strictly **out-of-sample** — the 3M yield is the only test input, and we never peek at the actual values of the yields we are trying to predict.\n"
      ]
    },
